  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules set a 7% permanent test-failure limit with no mandatory sales stop, which keeps the Hearth 10 (6.2%) on the market while the 5% level only triggers a corrective-action plan; per-model results go to customers but not the public. The recall trigger is 8 per 100,000 with no transition or corrective alternative, which would force Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) into a recall, while the 36-month suppression and 6-year retrofit deadlines sit at or near the red lines. Section S3 is weakened mainly because new-unit shut-off is allowed 36 months after adoption rather than within 12 months."
 },
